    "title": "Noise core vectors",
    "sections": ["14.1", "16.1", "16.2", "16.3 F15", "3.4", "6.5", "8.1"],
    "summary": "The published cacophony and snow vector sets for Noise_IK_25519_ChaChaPoly_SHA256 and Noise_NX_25519_ChaChaPoly_SHA256, transcoded into the §16.2 corpus format. §14.1 makes reproducing them a MUST for the first-party Noise state machine.",
    "transcodeRule": "Every value below is copied verbatim from its upstream vector. Nothing here was computed, regenerated, normalised, or reordered by this repository: the upstream hex strings are already lowercase, and the only restructuring is splitting each vector's flat `messages` array into the two handshake messages of the pattern and the transport messages that follow, and renaming fields to the §16.1 testOnly convention.",
    "messageOrder": "Both patterns are two-message patterns, so upstream messages 0 and 1 are the handshake (initiator, then responder) and every later message is a transport message, alternating initiator, responder, initiator, responder. Transport messages are encrypted under the Split() outputs — the first for initiator-to-responder, the second for responder-to-initiator (§6.5) — each with its own counter starting at zero and an empty AD.",
    "sharedTestKeyMaterial": "None. Unlike a generated family, each upstream vector carries its own key material, so it is stated per case under inputs.testOnly*."
  },
